#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
What Problem: Test runs block agents — `test-run` runs synchronously, the agent
is idle during the test window. For long suites (BATS + vitest + XCTest
combined can be 30s+) that's a lot of wasted agent context. The Monitor tool
(Claude Code v2.1.98+) can watch a background script and react to output
lines in real-time, enabling the agent to keep designing while tests run.

How & Why: test-monitor is a Python 3.13 tool that shells out to test-run
(or frameworks directly), parses their output via framework-specific
plugins (agency/tools/lib/test_parsers/), and emits monitor-tool-family-
convention `[TEST <suite>]` line events on stdout. Each stdout line becomes
a Monitor notification to the agent. On run completion, emits a `[TEST]
run complete` line carrying the exit code — /quality-gate Step 8 reads
that to gate the QG.

This is Iteration 1 of test-monitor v1. BATS support only. No triggers
yet (Iter 3), no state file (Iter 3), no file-watch (Iter 5). The design
is in agency/workstreams/devex/test-monitor-ad-20260419.md.

Usage:
    ./agency/tools/test-monitor                    # run all suites from agency.yaml
    ./agency/tools/test-monitor --suite tools      # run a single suite
    ./agency/tools/test-monitor --verbose          # also emit CASE_PASS lines
    ./agency/tools/test-monitor --timeout 120      # kill subprocess after 120s

Python: 3.13+ (framework floor per D45-R1). Stdlib only for framework tools
(ZERO-PIP CONSTRAINT). Shebang convention: `#!/usr/bin/env python3` + runtime
`sys.version_info` guard (not `python3.13`).

Written: 2026-04-19 devex — test-monitor Iter 1.
Renamed: 2026-04-22 — v46 Great Rename (claude/ → agency/, tests/ → src/tests/).
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import sys

